The C++/WinRT package provides CMake targets:

    find_package(cppwinrt CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Microsoft::CppWinRT)

This overlay port (Linux/macOS-host cross-compile only) generates the
`-base` subset only: winrt/base.h and the winrt/impl/* support
headers, sufficient for winrt::com_ptr and other base COM interop. It
does not generate OS-namespace projection headers (winrt/Windows.*.h),
since that needs real Windows SDK .winmd metadata that an xwin sysroot
does not provide. See examples/linux-cross-compile/README.md (in the
CommonLibSSE-NG submodule) for the underlying toolchain.
